# CrossTown

A multi-modal spatial transit accessibility and equity analytics platform for Henrico County, VA. CrossTown analyzes walkability, transit access, and demographic coverage using PostGIS, FastAPI, and MapLibre GL JS.

---

## Prerequisites

Before setting up the project locally, ensure you have installed:
* [Python 3.10+](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
* [PostgreSQL 15+](https://www.postgresql.org/download/) with the **PostGIS** extension installed
* [Git](https://git-scm.com/)

---

## 1. Project Setup & Virtual Environment

1. **Clone the Repository:**
   ```powershell
   git clone [https://github.com/virajkdrhs/CrossTown.git](https://github.com/virajkdrhs/CrossTown.git)
   cd CrossTown
Create and Activate a Python Virtual Environment (venv):

Windows (PowerShell):

PowerShell
python -m venv venv
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
(If you get a script execution policy error, run Set-ExecutionPolicy -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope Process once).

Mac / Linux:

Bash
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
Install Dependencies:

PowerShell
pip install -r requirements.txt
2. Linking Data Files (Google Drive)
To keep the repository lightweight, raw spatial data (.pbf, .zip, .shp) and intermediate processed datasets are hosted in our team Google Drive folder.

Download the shared data folder from our Team Google Drive Link (Insert actual Drive link here).

Extract the downloaded folder into the root directory of your local CrossTown project so your workspace looks like this:

Plaintext
CrossTown/
├── backend/
│   ├── main.py
│   └── load_to_postgis.py
├── frontend/
│   ├── index.html
│   └── app.js
├── data/                       <-- Place downloaded Google Drive files here
│   ├── virginia-latest.osm.pbf
│   ├── Henrico_BlockGroups_CarFree.geojson
│   └── County_Parks.geojson
├── venv/                       (Ignored by Git)
├── .gitignore
├── README.md
└── requirements.txt
3. Database & Spatial Ingestion Setup
Open pgAdmin or PostgreSQL terminal and create a database named crosstown:

SQL
CREATE DATABASE crosstown;
\c crosstown;
CREATE EXTENSION postgis;
Update your local database password in backend/load_to_postgis.py and backend/main.py:

Python
DB_PASS = "YOUR_LOCAL_POSTGRES_PASSWORD"
Run the ingestion script to populate PostgreSQL/PostGIS tables with spatial layers and access grid points:

PowerShell
python backend/load_to_postgis.py
4. Running the Application
A. Start the FastAPI Backend
With (venv) active in your terminal, run:

PowerShell
uvicorn backend.main:app --reload
The backend API will start at http://127.0.0.1:8000. You can view interactive API documentation at http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs.

B. Launch the Frontend Map
Open VS Code.

Open frontend/index.html using the Live Server extension (or open the file directly in your web browser).

The MapLibre map will load the 0–100 accessibility grid overlay and Census demographic layers directly from your local FastAPI backend.

Team Workflow & Git Etiquette
Always pull the latest changes before starting work:

PowerShell
git pull origin main
Do not commit local .env files, large dataset downloads (.pbf, .zip), or the venv/ folder. They are automatically handled by .gitignore.


---

### Step to Push the README to GitHub:

Once you save `README.md`, push it to GitHub with these commands in your PowerShell terminal:

```powershell
git add .
git commit -m "Add README with team setup instructions and data linking guide"
git push
Your repository home page on GitHub will now display formatted setup instructions for your team.
